# CODEOWNERS — EOS agentic-governance protection (SCAFFOLD)
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS [audit E1/H5]
#   Without CODEOWNERS + branch protection, anyone with write access — or an agent granted
#   `editFiles` — can change the files that steer every AI action (instructions, agents, hooks,
#   CI) WITHOUT review. A poisoned instruction could merge unreviewed. This file routes those
#   paths to required reviewers so self-/silent modification of governance is blocked.
#
# HONEST SCOPE — a template CANNOT enforce server-side settings.
#   This file only has EFFECT if the downstream repo ALSO enables, on GitHub (Settings > Branches):
#     • Branch protection on the default branch
#     • "Require a pull request before merging" + "Require review from Code Owners"
#     • (recommended) "Require status checks to pass" → select the `verify` job so the 3 CI hard
#       gates (validate-config / eos-doctor / secret-scan) become authoritative, not just advisory.
#   Until you enable those, CODEOWNERS is advisory only. Steps: see docs/eos/user-manual.md
#   → "Post-instantiation hardening (make the gates authoritative)".
#
# ACTION ON INSTANTIATION
#   Replace @niaodian everywhere below with your team handle (e.g. @your-org/platform-team).
#   A team handle is preferred over a person so review isn't blocked when one person is away.

# Default owner for everything (more specific rules below win).
*                                   @niaodian

# --- Agentic governance: the files that steer every AI action. Protect hardest. ---
/.github/                           @niaodian
/.github/copilot-instructions.md    @niaodian
/.github/instructions/              @niaodian
/.github/agents/                    @niaodian
/.github/prompts/                   @niaodian
/.github/hooks/                     @niaodian
/.github/eos/                       @niaodian
/.github/workflows/                 @niaodian
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @niaodian
/AGENTS.md                          @niaodian

# --- Workflow spine: gate definitions, gate policy and the action→agent map decide what is
#     enforced and what a developer is told to do next. Changing them invalidates prior evidence
#     by design, so they must never be self-modifiable without review.
/.eos/project.json                  @niaodian
/.eos/gates.json                    @niaodian
/.eos/workflow.json                 @niaodian
/.eos/agent-map.json                @niaodian
/.eos/schemas/                      @niaodian
/.eos/waivers/                      @niaodian
/.eos/ledger/                       @niaodian

# --- EOS spine + security/compliance docs: changes alter the methodology itself. ---
